# M6 4a (slice 345; Codex CODEX-OPUS-345-4A-REPLY-20261110T041147Z-01 item 1): `a := value` among the actuals of a call
# is no named actual any more and no positional value: the binder refuses the call before any actual is evaluated (5),
# so touch() never runs; native and forced code leave there as well. The named actual is written `a: value`
# (named_arguments).
fn: touch () int (int: calls 0)
    calls: calls + 1
    return: 1
end: touch
fn: tst (int: c 3; int: a 2) int
    return: c * 10 + a
end: tst
int: result tst(a := touch())
int: after touch\var\calls
